>So? Sokoban or conflict 

Sokoban only has a 50/50 chance of getting you reflection.  Conflict
won't save you if you happen to step into the line of sight of an
intelligent monster armed with a wand of death; only displacement,
invisibility, an excellent AC, magic resistance, or reflection will do
that.  Furthermore, Conflict runs the risk that one of the quest
hostiles will attack your nemesis and wake them.  Finally, monsters may
resist the effects of a ring of conflict if they have non-zero magic
resistance.

Also, the Samurai quest is one of the few occasions where I'd rather
wear an amulet of life saving than any other amulet; the odds of
Ashikaga Takauji scoring *two* bisecting hits are much lower than the
odds of him scoring *one*.  There are, after all, other sources of
reflection.

Overall, the only nemesis I'd be even vaguely tempted to attempt this
attack against would be Master Kaen (since the EotO are quite nice, and
he is brutally hard).  After all, as things stand, the Tsurugi of
Muramasa sucks big fat hairy ones anyway.  It's a two-handed weapon (so
if it gets cursed, *both* your hands stick to it), amulet thieves can
steal it if you are a Samurai, and while it does do a lot of damage, it
doesn't do anything like as much as it used to back in 3.1.3.

Excalibur two-weaponed with a katana, or wielded in combination with a
shield of reflection, is a much better option for a Samurai in pretty
much all circumstances.

